COMMENT     PROVISIONAL REFSEQ: This record has not yet been subject to final
            NCBI review. The reference sequence was derived from FJ858267.
            URL -- http://www.jgi.doe.gov/MicromonasRCC299
            JGI Project ID: 4000189
            Source DNA available from Alexandra Z. Worden (azworden@mbari.org)
            Organism available from the Roscoff Culture Collection RCC299
            Contact: Alexandra Z. Worden (azworden@mbari.org)
            Annotation done by Elodie Foulon.
            This organism was isolated from South Pacific surface waters in
            1998 by S. Boulben. This strain was rendered clonal and axenic
            through a series of plating and antibiotic treatments.
            Subsequently, the axenic strain was deposited at the CCMP
            (CCMP2709) and RCC (RCC827).
            The JGI and collaborators endorse the principles for the
            distribution and use of large scale sequencing data adopted by the
            larger genome sequencing community and urge users of this data to
            follow them. We welcome collaborative interaction on the project.
            (http://www.genome.gov/page.cfm?pageID=10506376).
            COMPLETENESS: full length.
